# ==========================================================
# CELL 10 (v2)
# ITERATIVE LLM RELATIONSHIP / PREDICATE EXTRACTION
#
# MAIN LOGIC (unchanged):
#
#   SOURCE DOCUMENT TITLE
#          +
#   ONE TARGET HYPERLINK
#          +
#   SENTENCE CONTAINING TARGET
#          +
#   6-WORD LOCAL CONTEXT
#          |
#          v
#        LLM  (one call per target)
#          |
#          v
#    ONE PREDICATE  ->  ONE RDF TRIPLE
#
#
# WHAT CHANGED vs v1:
#
#   1. Chunked checkpointing: results are saved every
#      CHUNK_DOCS documents, so a crash never loses a whole run.
#   2. `status` column (ok / no_sentence / parse_error / failed).
#      API failures are no longer saved as fake "related_to" edges.
#      Documents with failed rows are re-processed on the next run.
#   3. No double LLM run: row counts come from the saved table,
#      not from re-evaluating the lazy DataFrame.
#   4. Threaded LLM calls inside each partition (much faster).
#   5. Robust sentence finder (finds target first, expands to the
#      nearest sentence boundary, ignores abbreviations such as
#      "e.g." and periods inside other <links>).
#   6. Retry / timeout / max_tokens on the LLM client.
#   7. Safer parsing (strength, descriptions containing the
#      delimiter, list-style responses, <=5-word predicates).
#   8. Improved prompt (triple direction, concrete examples,
#      `mentions` fallback) + small predicate alias map.
#   9. Optional secret-scope token, tableExists() check,
#      same-target-twice-in-a-document called only once.
#  10. `evidence_sentence` column for auditing each edge.
# ==========================================================


